<title>USA: USDA says 110,000 tns U.S. corn sold to Taiwan.</title>
<headline>USDA says 110,000 tns U.S. corn sold to Taiwan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private exporters have reported the sale of 110,000 tonnes of U.S. corn to Taiwan, U.S. Agriculture Department said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The sale includes 54,000 tonnes for delivery in the 1996-97 marketing year and 56,000 tonnes for delivery in 1997-98. The U.S. corn marketing year begins Sept 1.</p>
<p>Exporters are required to report grains sales of 100,000 tonnes or more in a single day to USDA.</p>
</text>
